    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Feature Description\n\n## Description\n\n**Summary:**  \nWhen sending messages from [TRIfA (ToxAndroidRefImpl)](https://github.com/zoff99/ToxAndroidRefImpl/) or Antidote (iOS) to aTox (and also qTox, especially with newer Qt6 versions), the received text appears with strange or corrupted characters. This issue does not occur with other major Tox clients, which handle the enhanced message format properly.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Send a message from TRIfA or Antidote (which use the enhanced text message format as described [here](https://github.com/zoff99/c-toxcore/blob/zoff99/zoxcore_local_fork/docs/message_v3_alternate_docs.md)) to aTox/qTox.  \n2. Observe the received message in aTox/qTox.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nMessages should be displayed correctly, preserving all characters and formatting as sent.\n\n## Actual Behavior\n\nMessages arrive with strange or corrupted characters, making them unreadable.\n\nOld screenshot reused from https://github.com/zoff99/ToxAndroidRefImpl/issues/325, ignore the date same issue today (2025-05-02):\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/54327956-77b8-4927-822e-81044d6af580)\n\n## Notes\n\n- This issue seems to be related to the enhanced text message format (message v3) used by TRIfA/Antidote.  \n- All other major Tox clients handle this format correctly.  \n- The issue is present in newer TokTok/qTox versions (Qt6), which may have different UTF-8 handling.  \n- The aTox author is aware of the issue but has not fixed it yet.  \n- The TokTok/qTox developers are currently discussing how to handle this, but no decision has been reached.\n\n## References\n\n- [Enhanced Message Format Documentation](https://github.com/zoff99/c-toxcore/blob/zoff99/zoxcore_local_fork/docs/message_v3_alternate_docs.md)  \n- [Original Issue in ToxAndroidRefImpl](https://github.com/zoff99/ToxAndroidRefImpl/issues/325)\n\n## Request\n\nCould you please investigate and add support for the enhanced message format in aTox/qTox so that messages from TRIfA and Antidote are displayed correctly?\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter!\n\n### Contribution\n\n- [ ] I would like to contribute to this feature",
